      "math_academy_id": "q-34970",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Let $P$ be a $7\\times 6$ matrix that has $4$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $P?$",
      "worked_solution": "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(P))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $P.$ \n\nSince $P$ has $6$ columns and $4$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $P$ is \n\n$$\n6-4=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(P))=2.$",
